---

When something here stops being true, correct it in the same commit that made
it false. A stale line reads as authority: on 2026-08-17 one claimed a tool
offered a commit around every phase when it had been disabled by config the
whole time, and three sessions read the claim as fact before anyone ran it.

Keep this file under 200 lines, the size Claude Code's memory docs target per
CLAUDE.md (code.claude.com/docs/en/memory, read 2026-10-05): longer files cost
context and reduce adherence, and an `@` import does not lower that cost. The
files loaded together — this one, the global rules, its imports — also have a
combined limit Claude Code warns about. So a rule added past the limit is not a
rule gained — it is an existing one diluted.
